 ("Can you create an object of an abstract class?", "No", "Yes", "Only on the heap", "Only with new[]", "You can have pointers or references to it."),
 ("Why make a base-class destructor virtual?", "So deleting through a base pointer runs the derived destructor", "To make the class abstract", "To speed up destruction", "To prevent copying", "Otherwise behaviour is undefined."),
 ("C++ solves the diamond problem with:", "Virtual inheritance", "Friend classes", "Templates", "Private inheritance", "One shared base subobject."),
 ("Default access of members in a C++ class is:", "private", "public", "protected", "Depends on the compiler", "In a struct it is public."),
 ("With class D : B { }; B is inherited as:", "private", "public", "protected", "virtual", "struct would default to public."),
 ("Which cannot be virtual in C++?", "A constructor", "A destructor", "A member function", "An overloaded operator member", "The object does not have a vptr yet."),
 ("Why must a copy constructor take its parameter by reference?", "Passing by value would call the copy constructor again, recursing forever", "For speed only", "Because of const rules", "References cannot be null", "Compilers reject by-value copy constructors."),
 ("The rule of three covers:", "Destructor, copy constructor, copy assignment", "Constructor, destructor, move", "new, delete, sizeof", "public, private, protected", "If you need one, you usually need all three."),
 ("A shallow copy of an object that owns a raw pointer risks:", "A double free", "A compile error", "Faster copies", "Stack overflow", "Both objects delete the same memory."),
 ("A friend function:", "Can access private members but is not a member", "Is a member function", "Is inherited", "Must be virtual", "Friendship is granted, not inherited."),
 ("A static data member is:", "Shared by all objects of the class", "Copied into each object", "Only visible in one file", "Constant", "Defined once."),
 ("Inside a static member function, this is:", "Not available", "A const pointer", "A null pointer", "The first object created", "It is not tied to any object."),
 ("Overriding requires that the derived function:", "Has the same signature as a virtual base function", "Has a different name", "Is static", "Has a different parameter list", "Use override so the compiler checks."),
 ("'Subtypes must be usable wherever the base type is' is which SOLID principle?", "Liskov substitution", "Open/closed", "Interface segregation", "Dependency inversion", "The L in SOLID."),
 ("'Open for extension, closed for modification' is the:", "Open/closed principle", "Single responsibility principle", "Liskov substitution principle", "Dependency inversion principle", "Add new behaviour without editing tested code."),
 ("Dependency inversion says high-level modules should depend on:", "Abstractions", "Concrete classes", "Global variables", "The database", "Both sides depend on interfaces."),
 ("Interface segregation says:", "Prefer several small interfaces to one large one", "Every class needs an interface", "Interfaces must not have methods", "Use multiple inheritance always", "Clients should not depend on methods they do not use."),
 ("A 'has-a' relationship is modelled by:", "Composition", "Inheritance", "Overloading", "Templates", "Inheritance models 'is-a'."),
 ("Which operator cannot be overloaded in C++?", "::", "+", "[]", "()", "Also . .* ?: and sizeof."),
 ("The Singleton pattern ensures:", "A class has one instance with a global access point", "A class cannot be inherited", "Objects are created through a factory", "Objects are immutable", "Often criticised for hidden global state."),
 ("The Factory pattern:", "Creates objects without the caller naming the concrete class", "Guarantees one instance", "Notifies many objects of a change", "Wraps an incompatible interface", "Callers depend on an interface."),
 ("Which pattern notifies many objects when one object's state changes?", "Observer", "Adapter", "Builder", "Singleton", "Publish and subscribe."),
 ("In a typical implementation, the vptr is stored:", "In each object of a class with virtual functions", "Once per class in the vtable", "In the stack frame", "In a global table per program", "Each object points to its class's vtable."),
